# whole-host record H4/W8/unenforced
# checkpoint v0.21.0, H4/W2: connectome-host 0.21.0, agent-framework 0.32.0, context-manager 0.24.0, membrane 0.8.0, chronicle 0.5.1, bun 1.4.4
# candidate: connectome-host 0.21.0, agent-framework 0.32.0, context-manager 0.24.0, membrane 0.8.0, chronicle 0.5.1, bun 1.4.4
templates
T:call-context-manager-cm = Context Manager: [CM] Recall memory L#-#.
T:call-context-manager-system = Context Manager: System: You will soon form a new memory, get ready. The messages that follow are the slice of recent experience you are about to compress. After them, write the memory in your own voice.
T:call-context-manager-write = Context Manager: Write the memory of events since the most recent memory system notification. Speak in the first person from your own perspective. Preserve concrete details — file paths, exact values, decisions, unresolved questions, the user's active asks. Target ~# tokens. Output only the memory body — no preamble, no section headers unless they help preservation, no meta-commentary about summarizing. Memorize only what actually happened in that slice: if it holds little beyond routine system traffic (heartbeats, empty turns, failure notices), a short memory saying so is correct — do not pad it by re-narrating events you already remember from earlier as if they had just happened again.
T:call-empty = 
  
  ---
  
  
T:call-routing-your-plain = [routing] Your plain speech now lands in chat. Other channels need an explicit send tool.
T:call-the-local-time = The local time at the start of this session is #-#-#T#:#:#.#+#:# [UTC].
T:call-user-clock-monday = user: Clock: Monday #-#-#, #:# UTC
T:call-user-delivered-plain = user: [delivered] plain speech → chat
T:subconscious-skip-reply = skip_reply {}
